WEBVTT

00:01.750 --> 00:05.430
We're allied with the all-powerful 
Moz-sensei just for now.

00:05.430 --> 00:09.730
Dress up as an intruder and beat the 
crap out of the enemy soldiers!

01:52.270 --> 01:57.010
<b>Battle in Three Dimensions</b>

01:58.650 --> 02:02.230
No, the hooded warriors 
were more than just strong!

02:02.230 --> 02:05.170
They pushed back against my miracle power!

02:05.170 --> 02:06.960
They might be as strong as Moz.

02:06.960 --> 02:12.200
There were three, five... no, ten of the 
hooded warriors attacking me with spears,

02:09.470 --> 02:11.440
<i>It </i>is<i> me, though.</i>

02:11.440 --> 02:15.160
<i>He can be weirdly perceptive,
although he's fundamentally an idiot.</i>

02:12.200 --> 02:15.160
and I fought them back with my miracle 
counterattack, all on my own!

02:15.160 --> 02:18.860
Then they attacked me 
with this flash of light,

02:15.770 --> 02:18.860
Go for the confident, strong men.

02:18.860 --> 02:20.730
They'll make you sound really awesome

02:18.860 --> 02:26.250
so I casually picked up a heavy boulder with 
one arm and... Zap! Zap! I was stunned.

02:20.730 --> 02:23.030
so they don't have to make 
themselves sound weak.

02:27.040 --> 02:32.140
Now, our happy conspiracy 
operation is super simple.

02:32.480 --> 02:34.800
Once the enemy's thoroughly freaked out

02:35.270 --> 02:39.800
by our ridiculously strong 
imaginary hooded warrior...

02:39.800 --> 02:40.550
First,

02:40.950 --> 02:45.810
we'll discreetly set our aerial combat 
drone up at a good spot for takeoff.

02:46.030 --> 02:46.560
Second...

02:48.240 --> 02:50.260
The hooded warriors are here!

02:50.260 --> 02:51.390
Over there!

02:52.180 --> 02:52.690
Third...

02:53.190 --> 02:55.570
Take them all out with the 
petrification weapon!

02:55.570 --> 02:56.320
Fourth...

02:57.560 --> 02:58.820
Oh, no!

02:59.950 --> 03:02.410
I hope it works out like that.

03:02.410 --> 03:04.640
Nothing's ever gone to plan for us.

03:04.640 --> 03:06.640
You're always so unlucky.

03:07.130 --> 03:08.830
There's no other way to do it.

03:10.950 --> 03:14.500
I'm sure you're aware that 
there's one big problem.

03:15.360 --> 03:16.370
Moz.

03:16.860 --> 03:19.720
He'll surely be at the final battle.

03:19.720 --> 03:20.640
Am I right?

03:21.930 --> 03:26.770
If those hooded warriors 
are really that strong,

03:26.770 --> 03:29.890
Kirisame and I will go 
defeat them ourselves.

03:29.890 --> 03:31.140
Really?!

03:31.140 --> 03:34.520
Awesome! It's a Moz-san and 
Kirisame-san tag team!

03:34.520 --> 03:36.320
They're unbeatable!

03:37.530 --> 03:43.020
And the moment our drone takes 
the petrification weapon,

03:43.430 --> 03:45.970
Moz will kill us all and take it for himself.

03:48.190 --> 03:52.160
That's why we're working 
on a counter-Moz plan.

03:54.320 --> 03:56.570
Such a waste!

03:56.570 --> 04:01.720
We're chopping up my dear 
glass-blowing steel pipes?

04:02.830 --> 04:07.510
Once we cut them into short macaroni-shaped 
tubes, we'll put eight of them together.

04:07.510 --> 04:09.850
It just goes round and round.

04:09.850 --> 04:11.180
A fidget spinner?!

04:11.180 --> 04:12.040
Another one?

04:12.040 --> 04:17.610
Now that we've reinvented them, 
we'll put these new items to good use.

04:17.610 --> 04:21.540
I've built them as ordered, 
but what <i>are</i> these?

04:21.540 --> 04:24.310
I wanna keep working on the drone.

04:24.310 --> 04:28.740
He said it's a counter-Moz thing, so I 
was expecting some kind of sick weapon.

04:32.940 --> 04:35.370
Is this what I think it is?

04:36.650 --> 04:40.030
Looks like all the modern 
people recognize it.

04:40.030 --> 04:41.380
Damn it!

04:42.210 --> 04:45.450
Structurally, it's not that complex.

04:45.450 --> 04:46.580
There was even an incident

04:46.580 --> 04:50.690
where prisoners made one with 
the materials they had on hand.

04:50.690 --> 04:53.520
It's the internals that get a bit difficult.

04:54.130 --> 04:57.600
We pack gunpowder made from 
nitric acid in a small cylinder,

04:57.600 --> 05:00.270
shove a pachinko ball in there, and cap it.

05:01.530 --> 05:06.410
So then the gunpowder goes boom, 
and the ball goes fwoosh, right?

05:06.410 --> 05:08.850
This is one that I could figure out.

05:08.850 --> 05:11.480
It's not that complicated.

05:12.480 --> 05:17.390
You're on the right track, but who's 
going to light the gunpowder?

05:17.390 --> 05:19.190
What are we, making matchlocks?

05:19.190 --> 05:22.760
We need a detonator to smack 
the gunpowder and ignite it.

05:22.760 --> 05:25.120
We'll use mercury fulminate.

05:26.790 --> 05:29.830
There's no way I'm understanding 
any of that now.

05:29.830 --> 05:32.890
I take it back. This is still complicated.

05:32.890 --> 05:36.640
One wrong move, and we get blown up.

05:36.640 --> 05:38.790
I'll have to do this part myself.

05:39.350 --> 05:43.350
We just need to combine nitric 
acid, mercury, and alcohol.

05:43.350 --> 05:45.600
Then we just make it into a detonator,

05:45.600 --> 05:47.450
and we'll have bullets.

05:48.050 --> 05:50.820
Hit the detonator with a hammer, and...

05:54.620 --> 05:58.610
In the very beginning, Senku, 
Yuzuriha, and I traveled to Hakone

05:58.610 --> 06:01.090
because we had no choice but to make it.

06:01.790 --> 06:05.170
How many years has it been?

06:07.110 --> 06:08.930
About three years.

06:09.450 --> 06:12.950
It took a while, but this is 
where humanity always ends up.

06:14.470 --> 06:17.540
Now I'm definitely going to hell.

06:20.000 --> 06:23.540
This is what made men and 
women, young and old,

06:23.540 --> 06:28.120
all of humanity, of homo 
sapiens, the apex species.

06:28.120 --> 06:30.360
It's the invention of the gods and demons.

06:35.660 --> 06:37.990
Tools are neither gods nor demons.

06:38.490 --> 06:40.870
It's up to the person to 
determine how it's used.

06:44.320 --> 06:45.820
Sorry, everyone.

06:45.820 --> 06:49.510
I'm sure you don't want to be hearing 
platitudes at a time like this,

06:50.090 --> 06:54.140
but I still don't want to kill anyone.

06:55.030 --> 06:56.600
So let's hold back—

06:56.600 --> 06:57.820
Platitudes?

06:59.060 --> 07:00.750
You're wrong about that, Ukyo.

07:01.950 --> 07:04.800
To not kill is neither a platitude nor ethics.

07:05.210 --> 07:08.280
Someone whose loved one is 
killed bears that grudge forever.

07:08.280 --> 07:13.210
We take even the enemy for ourselves.
To do that, we avoid killing.

07:13.210 --> 07:14.710
That's only rational.

07:18.170 --> 07:20.730
There's no way we're killing anyone, anyway.

07:20.730 --> 07:24.740
We didn't even put rifling 
in this makeshift gun.

07:24.740 --> 07:26.610
It's neither precise nor 
powerful enough to be

07:26.610 --> 07:28.400
more than a good-luck charm 
to make us feel better.

07:28.400 --> 07:31.390
I guess it could serve as a 
tranquilizer gun, in the best case.

07:31.850 --> 07:33.180
That's a tranquilizer?

07:33.630 --> 07:36.370
Doesn't matter if we hit them in the legs.

07:36.370 --> 07:38.610
Once we have the petrification device,

07:39.180 --> 07:43.190
we can stone them, melt them, 
and they're back to normal!

07:43.190 --> 07:46.190
It's basically a tranquilizer gun!

07:46.190 --> 07:49.090
Er, well, I guess so, but...

07:49.090 --> 07:50.920
You're becoming so pragmatic

07:50.920 --> 07:54.080
that you're starting to sound like 
a mad scientist, Senku-chan.

07:54.080 --> 07:55.820
He's always been that way.

07:56.210 --> 07:59.730
I see you've made it pistol-sized so 
that it doesn't cause suspicion...

08:00.070 --> 08:01.420
But who's using it?

08:01.420 --> 08:04.070
It'll be a challenge for anyone 
who's never used a gun before.

08:04.070 --> 08:06.280
How many people in Japan could...

08:11.170 --> 08:13.180
m 0 0 l 198 0 l 198 80 l 0 80

08:11.170 --> 08:13.180
Yo
returns!!

08:14.700 --> 08:17.610
We'll have an officer in active 
service handle the gun.

08:17.610 --> 08:20.310
That works for you, right, Ukyo?

08:20.310 --> 08:22.380
No, that's a bad idea!

08:22.380 --> 08:25.930
Giving this asshole such a badass weapon?

08:27.380 --> 08:28.840
His face...

08:29.190 --> 08:32.050
Yeah, you can see it in his face!

08:32.050 --> 08:33.570
He's a piece of shit!

08:34.020 --> 08:36.080
Nah, not really.

08:36.080 --> 08:40.360
Yo's just a happy-go-lucky guy with 
an oversized need for validation.

08:40.360 --> 08:43.460
That kinda makes him the 
easiest type to control.

08:43.820 --> 08:46.480
The first sheriff of the new world!

08:46.480 --> 08:49.090
It's history in the making.

08:57.520 --> 08:58.570
Oh, my...

08:58.570 --> 09:01.220
You're so impressive.

09:03.930 --> 09:05.050
Your face!

09:08.930 --> 09:11.320
Nothing I can't handle!

09:11.320 --> 09:14.870
I used to shoot bullies and shit!

09:14.870 --> 09:16.700
That's... bad, right?

09:16.700 --> 09:17.700
That's bad.

09:42.320 --> 09:43.070
Huh?

09:43.420 --> 09:45.380
None of them hit.

09:45.380 --> 09:49.730
Come on, he put on such a smug face 
shooting, and missed every shot.

09:54.790 --> 09:56.010
A venomous snake!

09:56.500 --> 09:59.070
Crap, is it because that showed up?

10:00.860 --> 10:06.560
It looks like we're beyond being 
mere prey to be hunted down.

10:06.560 --> 10:07.690
Am I right?

10:08.960 --> 10:11.420
m 0 0 l 198 0 l 198 80 l 0 80

10:08.960 --> 10:11.420
Gun
acquired!!

10:12.040 --> 10:14.890
Good going, outlaw policeman.

10:16.460 --> 10:17.760
<i>I can't tell them!</i>

10:17.760 --> 10:21.430
<i>I can't tell them I was just 
shooting for the bottles!</i>

10:21.640 --> 10:24.200
<i>I gotta practice like mad!</i>

10:31.250 --> 10:35.690
In order to defeat the Medusa, 
we need four pieces of equipment.

10:36.250 --> 10:40.990
Let's get them all done and start our mission.

10:36.670 --> 10:40.990
Hoods

10:37.050 --> 10:40.990
Drone

10:37.420 --> 10:40.990
Guns

10:37.800 --> 10:40.990
Wires

10:41.450 --> 10:45.230
We'll set decoy hoods in front of the enemy.

10:45.230 --> 10:49.090
We need her to throw the petrification 
weapon ten billion percent of the time,

10:49.090 --> 10:50.590
or we're doomed.

10:50.590 --> 10:51.510
Yeah.

10:51.850 --> 10:53.910
We'll want at least five.

10:57.700 --> 10:59.580
It's strange...

10:59.580 --> 11:03.960
The food and clothes in storage 
keep going missing lately.

11:06.330 --> 11:08.310
Hoods

11:07.330 --> 11:08.310
<b>Complete</b>

11:11.270 --> 11:12.530
<i>Oh, yeah...</i>

11:12.530 --> 11:17.070
<i>We're going to need to camouflage all 
the work noise that's going on lately.</i>

11:23.460 --> 11:25.750
Amaryllis! Why are you here?

11:25.750 --> 11:26.970
Did you come from the inner palace?

11:26.970 --> 11:28.820
Don't tell anyone!

11:31.040 --> 11:33.250
I ran away.

11:34.050 --> 11:40.800
I couldn't forget about the three of 
you who proposed so powerfully to me.

11:41.130 --> 11:45.100
I'll elope with the strongest man here.

11:45.100 --> 11:51.540
For example, with the man who can bang 
the drum the hardest at the next festival!

11:52.740 --> 11:54.560
<i>I took it too far!</i>

11:54.560 --> 11:56.400
<i>This isn't going to work.</i>

11:59.710 --> 12:01.990
<i>Nope, that totally worked.</i>

12:13.060 --> 12:15.280
I can practice now!

12:15.280 --> 12:17.950
I'm finally shooting pretty straight!

12:18.130 --> 12:19.760
<b>Guns</b>

12:19.000 --> 12:19.760
<b>Complete</b>

12:20.200 --> 12:26.010
So, supposing we use this insane 
"gun" thing to slow Moz down...

12:26.010 --> 12:28.810
How do we take the all-important 
petrification device?

12:28.810 --> 12:31.170
You said it'd be an aerial 
battle using our drone,

12:31.170 --> 12:33.890
but what are we going to do 
with that raggedy-ass drone?

12:34.550 --> 12:39.650
She's got it on a rope, too, so the 
best we can really do is nab the rope.

12:39.650 --> 12:42.650
Bingo. Ten billion points to you.

12:42.990 --> 12:47.530
Which means it's going to 
be a tug-o-war in the end.

12:47.530 --> 12:48.780
Which is why...

12:49.180 --> 12:50.640
Wake up, y'all!

12:50.640 --> 12:52.760
The power team's up!

12:53.160 --> 12:56.040
m 0 0 l 138 0 l 138 60 l 0 60

12:53.160 --> 12:56.040
Magma is
revived!!

12:53.160 --> 12:56.040
m 0 0 l 138 0 l 138 60 l 0 60

12:53.160 --> 12:56.040
Nikki is
revived!!

12:53.160 --> 12:56.040
m 0 0 l 138 0 l 138 60 l 0 60

12:53.160 --> 12:56.040
Kinro is
revived!!

13:02.700 --> 13:03.970
Tell me.

13:03.970 --> 13:05.340
I'm ready to hear it.

13:06.730 --> 13:09.640
Something's happened to Ginro, correct?

13:16.010 --> 13:17.150
I'm sorry.

13:18.130 --> 13:20.270
It happened right in front of me.

13:29.420 --> 13:31.560
You thought he was dead, didn't you?

13:32.320 --> 13:33.070
Yeah.

13:34.420 --> 13:36.190
He's barely alive.

13:36.190 --> 13:38.070
Thanks to Kohaku's quick thinking.

13:39.250 --> 13:39.970
Yeah....

13:40.810 --> 13:45.250
Kinro, we'll have you be the 
leader of the hooded warriors.

13:45.990 --> 13:50.720
We need a real spearman for the battle, 
or they'll know they aren't that strong.

13:52.420 --> 13:57.270
The lead spearman is ten billion percent 
going to get taken out by Moz or Kirisame.

13:59.910 --> 14:00.810
Yeah.

14:01.630 --> 14:02.900
That's fine.

14:06.700 --> 14:08.400
I'm going to save them.

14:09.860 --> 14:13.090
I'm going to win this 
battle and save them all!

14:14.200 --> 14:17.690
All right! Let's start practicing tugging!

14:17.690 --> 14:20.460
Go, power team!

14:21.200 --> 14:25.340
That's why we've got the science 
crafts team working on that.

14:27.020 --> 14:29.070
It's the cotton candy machine!

14:30.050 --> 14:31.370
It stinks, though.

14:31.370 --> 14:33.100
What's this black goo?

14:34.220 --> 14:36.460
Sadly, we can't eat that stuff.

14:36.460 --> 14:38.370
It's the leftovers of burnt coal.

14:38.370 --> 14:39.350
Tar.

14:39.660 --> 14:42.900
Spin this black cotton candy around, and...

14:44.140 --> 14:46.680
We have tough, light rope.

14:46.480 --> 14:50.070
<b>Wires</b>

14:46.680 --> 14:48.920
It's the birth of carbon wire!

14:48.900 --> 14:50.070
<b>Complete</b>

14:50.550 --> 14:52.490
Sure, yeah.

14:52.490 --> 14:54.240
Which means...

14:54.910 --> 14:56.520
Here we go again!

14:56.520 --> 14:59.750
The arduous endless spinning job!

15:02.290 --> 15:05.130
Senku, about this top...

15:05.130 --> 15:08.890
Why is it so stable even though 
it's spinning mid-air?

15:09.450 --> 15:11.050
That's the gyroscopic effect.

15:11.700 --> 15:14.610
Anything spinning really fast is stable.

15:14.610 --> 15:19.060
It's why bikes don't fall over and 
why the planet doesn't teeter.

15:19.060 --> 15:20.120
Here we go!

15:20.120 --> 15:23.690
I've got one of my crazy ideas!

15:24.130 --> 15:27.870
You know how our Mk 1 drone is shaky as hell?

15:28.570 --> 15:32.270
Yeah, it's just an electric 
bamboo copter right now.

15:33.390 --> 15:34.600
It's all good!

15:34.600 --> 15:37.450
We're all about trial and error here.

15:37.770 --> 15:41.990
Maybe if we put a fidget spinner 
in the middle of the drone,

15:41.990 --> 15:45.250
it'll stabilize it with that 
gyro-whatchamacallit effect.

15:46.370 --> 15:47.930
You're right!

15:47.930 --> 15:53.550
It's ten billion times simpler than making a 
pain-in-the-ass controller device, but not bad!

15:55.050 --> 15:56.810
And so...

15:56.810 --> 16:00.250
That's why our Mk 2 drone 
here has that built in.

16:00.250 --> 16:02.310
Blargh!

16:04.190 --> 16:07.130
Wow, it's so much more stable than before!

16:07.570 --> 16:10.320
And finally, we give it one of these!

16:13.040 --> 16:16.110
I don't know what that is, 
but it's another spinny thing!

16:16.110 --> 16:18.650
We have more spinny work again!

16:18.650 --> 16:21.970
You're completely traumatized 
by having to do spinny work.

16:21.970 --> 16:25.330
Yeah, we're making one for each propeller.

16:25.330 --> 16:33.220
m 0 0 l 250 0 l 250 60 l 0 60

16:25.330 --> 16:33.220
<b>Wirewound Variable Resistor</b>

16:25.700 --> 16:28.360
This is what's called a 
wirewound variable resistor.

16:28.360 --> 16:29.910
That's a long-ass name!

16:29.910 --> 16:33.220
You move the dial around to control 
how much electricity goes through.

16:33.640 --> 16:38.450
In other words, say we raise the 
voltage just to that propeller there.

16:39.740 --> 16:41.220
Damn, it moved!

16:41.650 --> 16:46.880
We aren't using these four knobs to steer 
it and keep it balanced manually, are we?

16:46.880 --> 16:48.380
We sure are.

16:48.790 --> 16:51.320
That's way too hard.

16:52.130 --> 16:57.210
You'd need to be good at steering 
and at reading the wind.

16:57.740 --> 16:58.530
Who's...

17:01.140 --> 17:02.290
I figured.

17:07.830 --> 17:09.620
I'm getting pretty good at this!

17:10.170 --> 17:11.370
<i>Is this guy for real?</i>

17:13.720 --> 17:15.320
It's not much different from gaming.

17:15.640 --> 17:19.200
I used to receive pro-gamer 
training as a child.

17:19.200 --> 17:20.630
<i>I forgot.</i>

17:20.630 --> 17:23.930
<i>This guy cheats at everything 
using the power of money.</i>

17:24.200 --> 17:27.320
Yo, what's up? That looks fun.

17:27.320 --> 17:30.000
Your shooter looks pretty fun, too.

17:30.000 --> 17:32.690
Quit messing around. This is practice time.

17:32.690 --> 17:34.580
We <i>are</i> practicing!

17:36.610 --> 17:38.870
<b>Drone</b>

17:37.360 --> 17:38.870
<b>Complete</b>

17:40.030 --> 17:42.870
Anyway, we have all our equipment now.

17:43.470 --> 17:47.020
We start right at sunrise.

17:48.970 --> 17:53.240
The battlefield is here, 
the cliff of the howling seas.

18:02.670 --> 18:09.010
The waves and wind are loud enough here 
that they'll drown out the drone.

18:16.310 --> 18:18.730
They've arrived at the 
cliff of the howling seas.

18:18.730 --> 18:22.120
It's the powerful hooded 
warriors we heard about.

18:23.200 --> 18:28.290
Looks like Kirisame and I are going 
to have to go fight them off.

18:29.180 --> 18:30.410
Move out, everyone!

18:30.410 --> 18:32.470
Beat them down!

18:33.710 --> 18:37.400
With my miracle power, and with 
Moz and Kirisame by my side,

18:37.400 --> 18:39.380
I, Oarashi, will not be defeated!

18:47.820 --> 18:50.100
All the enemies are on the way.

18:50.100 --> 18:52.830
We won't stand a chance 
against so many of them.

18:52.830 --> 18:57.360
Yeah, we'd get reamed, ten billion 
percent, if we faced them head-on.

18:59.720 --> 19:00.860
Let's be clear.

19:01.450 --> 19:07.250
Our only winning condition is to have the 
enemy throw the petrification device.

19:07.750 --> 19:11.310
If they don't, there's no 
aerial battle to speak of.

19:11.310 --> 19:13.880
Don't worry, Suika.

19:15.180 --> 19:18.840
Once we raid them from the air and 
catch the petrification device,

19:19.410 --> 19:25.580
we'll get the power team hiding in the 
lab car to yank it over, no matter what.

19:25.580 --> 19:26.690
We got this!

19:26.690 --> 19:27.560
Yeah!

19:27.840 --> 19:33.170
Finally, we'll neutralize them using the 
petrification device and your gun, Yo.

19:33.890 --> 19:35.150
Leave it to me!

19:35.150 --> 19:38.360
The biggest threat is the third force, Moz.

19:39.130 --> 19:40.130
Be careful.

19:40.490 --> 19:42.240
He'll only be on our side in the beginning.

19:42.240 --> 19:45.160
As soon as we draw the 
petrification device toward us,

19:45.520 --> 19:48.660
he'll become a powerful enemy 
bent on killing us all.

19:50.180 --> 19:55.650
Gathered here is the Petrification 
Kingdom, who is trying to eliminate us;

19:56.470 --> 20:00.130
us, the Kingdom of Science, who are 
here to take the petrification device;

20:00.860 --> 20:04.890
and the all-powerful warrior Moz, 
who wants both us and the device gone.

20:05.880 --> 20:07.290
Here we go.

20:07.680 --> 20:10.710
Time for the three-way final battle.

20:18.120 --> 20:19.940
They're here!

21:09.660 --> 21:15.610
We're mobilizing all of our scientific 
equipment to catch the Medusa.

21:31.810 --> 21:36.020
Miracle Power Revenge!

21:36.320 --> 21:38.770
Shit, he's charging right at us!

21:39.170 --> 21:42.830
Brute force is the best course 
of action for them, after all.

21:42.830 --> 21:45.980
Meatheads are stupid strong 
in these situations.

21:46.340 --> 21:48.780
I should have learned 
that from Taiju, damn it!

21:49.880 --> 21:51.120
I'll handle this.

21:53.700 --> 21:58.340
Indeed, it isn't for a silly deal this time.

21:58.720 --> 22:00.570
It's for a true battle.

22:00.910 --> 22:02.090
For myself.

22:02.690 --> 22:09.990
With this golden, sun-colored spear prepared 
for me by the Kingdom of Science...

22:12.250 --> 22:13.580
I will protect us!

23:49.400 --> 23:52.490
Total War

